      "evidence": "The claimed skipped log does not occur: RlsGuardRunner and ReadOnlyGuardRunner re-raise the rls.py scope-analysis and readonly.py dialect refusals from an RlsError/UnsafeSqlError, so the redactor logs them (VC-32 traced the same). The real defect was the reverse (relation check's ParseError fail-closed path logged twice) and the docstring overstating; _logged_by_guard now treats only a guard-refusal cause as unlogged, docstring rewritten. Criterion 26 (one WARNING record with the full reason) holds. Test: test_relation_check_parse_failure_is_not_logged_twice."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "VC-78",
      "decision": "applied",
      "commit": "851d85ecb410f0b723a2b651dc6d816c1d5ec6dd",
      "evidence": "check_catalog now checks every (table, column) pair across all sets, reporting each table-level problem once. Criterion 6 (a listed column missing makes serve/validate --check-db fail naming it) now holds for a column listed only by a later set. Test: test_catalog_check_covers_a_table_listed_again_by_a_later_set; MySQL connector suite 65 passed."
    }
